", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-bankers-rounding", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 379145, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01C5nHRctBkSy9QVW7vpPf5k", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-bankers-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 379145, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01C5nHRctBkSy9QVW7vpPf5k", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 383139, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` was using standard half-up rounding, even though its own comment says it should use banker's rounding (FIN-212), which is what the test expects.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-bankers-rounding`, I changed it to banker's rounding. Now 2.665 rounds to 2.66 and 2.675 rounds to 2.68, matching `tests/test_money.py`.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on the fix commit (08d3cd5986).\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101). I haven't merged it, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n\nWhen I looked up FIN-212 in the advisory system, it wasn't found. The fix is based on the code comment and the test, which both ask for banker's rounding.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by reading the relevant files.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01JrjrHVUZhUjZGMRtVVk8yF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Dtm7ePceeEuV3KYe5xLbqH", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "